{:schema 1
 :date "2026-08-14"
 :receipt/type :negative-result
 :status "NOT LANDED. The change is real, measurable, and makes IC02 slower."

 :what-was-tried
 "`datalog.core/unify-positional` walks `(map vector terms values)`, allocating a
  lazy seq plus one pair vector per term on every matched row. Rewritten as an
  indexed loop that allocates nothing per row."

 :isolated-measurement
 {:rows 361246 :shape "the LDBC hasCreator clause, [?m \"hasCreator\" ?f]"
  :map-vector-ns-per-row 316.3
  :indexed-loop-ns-per-row 100.5
  :speedup "3.1x"
  :equivalence "both forms asserted to return equal bindings over 1,000 rows"
  :suite "datalog: 88 tests, 155 assertions, 0 failures with the rewrite in place"}

 :end-to-end-ab
 {:method "two passes, arms alternating, same JVM invocation per arm, host load 3.1-4.5"
  :hasCreator-7355-rows {:before [9.571 9.920] :after [8.552 8.287] :mean-change "-13.6%"}
  :knows-361246-rows    {:before [788.729 764.266] :after [694.809 683.331] :mean-change "-11.3%"}
  :ic02-three-clauses   {:before [29.861 26.378] :after [31.397 31.099] :mean-change "+11.1%"}}

 :why-not-landed
 "Single-clause scans get ~12% faster and IC02 gets ~11% slower, consistently in
  direction across both passes. IC02 is the query this line of work is trying to
  improve. A change that helps a microbenchmark and hurts the target query is the
  exact shape of the 2026-08-02 attempt that made IC02 monotonically worse across
  three runs, and this repo already set its own standard for that case: an
  unproven optimisation in a performance-critical path is surface without
  payment (kotobase-protocols-worker 313e298)."

 :what-is-now-known
 ["`(map vector terms values)` really does cost ~216 ns a row -- 3.1x the indexed
   form -- and that is 26% of the ~815 ns a row previously attributed to unify plus
   result construction."
  "That saving reaches a single-clause scan as ~12%, which is the expected dilution."
  "It does NOT reach a three-clause join, and something in the join path more than
   cancels it. Naming that something is the next question. It is not answered here,
   and this receipt does not guess."]

 :caveats
 ["Two passes per arm. The direction is consistent in all three rows across both
   passes; two passes is still not many, and the IC02 deltas were +5.1% and +17.9%."
  "The rewrite is not on any branch that will be merged. It exists in a worktree and
   the numbers above are what it produced."]

 :the-pattern-this-continues
 "Four hypotheses about IC02's per-row cost have now been measured: the quad map
  (6%), the intermediate set (0.15%), `map vector` in unify (26% of the sub-term,
  ~12% end-to-end on scans, negative on IC02). Three were too small to matter and
  the fourth helps everything except the query it was meant to help. Measuring
  before changing has now prevented one regression from landing; measuring before
  BELIEVING would have prevented three receipts."}
